Now UI components.

`Screen.tsx`:
Need `edges` type. `SafeAreaView` from `react-native-safe-area-context` accepts `edges?: Edge[]`. Import `type Edge`.

```tsx
import type { ReactNode } from "react";
import { ScrollView, StyleSheet, View, type StyleProp, type ViewStyle } from "react-native";
import { SafeAreaView, type Edge } from "react-native-safe-area-context";
import { colors, spacing } from "@/theme/tokens";

interface ScreenProps { children: ReactNode; scroll?: boolean; padded?: boolean; edges?: Edge[]; style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>; }
```

If scroll, wrap in ScrollView with `contentContainerStyle={[styles.scrollContent, padded && styles.padded]}` and style prop on ScrollView? Use `style` for outer? Keep simple.

`Card.tsx`.
`StatusPill.tsx`.
`EmptyState.tsx`.
`PrimaryButton.tsx`.
`Field.tsx`.
`SectionHeader.tsx`.
`StatCard.tsx`.
`PlaceholderScreen.tsx` (domain).
`src/components/ui/index.ts` barrel.

Let's write them.

PrimaryButton:
```tsx
import { ActivityIndicator, Pressable, StyleSheet, Text } from "react-native";
import { colors, fontSize, radius, spacing } from "@/theme/tokens";

type Variant = "primary" | "danger" | "outline";

export function PrimaryButton({ label, onPress, loading = false, disabled = false, variant = "primary" }: {...}) {
  const isDisabled = disabled || loading;
  return (
    <Pressable
      accessibilityRole="button"
      accessibilityState={{ disabled: isDisabled, busy: loading }}
      disabled={isDisabled}
      onPress={onPress}
      style={({ pressed }) => [
        styles.base,
        variant === "danger" && styles.danger,
        variant === "outline" && styles.outline,
        (pressed || isDisabled) && styles.pressed,
      ]}
    >
      {loading ? <ActivityIndicator color={variant === "outline" ? colors.ink : colors.white} /> : <Text style={[styles.label, variant === "outline" && styles.outlineLabel]}>{label}</Text>}
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```
For danger text white. Primary white. Outline ink.
Styles.

Field:
```tsx
import { StyleSheet, Text, TextInput, View, type TextInputProps } from "react-native";
...
export function Field({ label, error, ...props }: TextInputProps & { label: string; error?: string }) {
  return (
    <View style={styles.wrapper}>
      <Text style={styles.label}>{label}</Text>
      <TextInput
        style={[styles.input, error ? styles.inputError : null, props.style]}
        placeholderTextColor={colors.mutedSoft}
        {...props}
      />
      {error ? <Text style={styles.error}>{error}</Text> : null}
    </View>
  );
}
```
Spreading props after style means `props.style` inside style array then `{...props}` would override style with `props.style` and lose defaults! Careful: destructure `style` out:
```tsx
export function Field({ label, error, style, ...props }) { ... <TextInput style={[styles.input, error && styles.inputError, style]} {...props} /> }
```
Good.

`StatCard`:
```tsx
