Need `ActivityIndicator` for loading state while session hydrates; if status loading, show splash. If authenticated, Redirect. But hooks must run before conditional return? We use useState before conditions; fine.

Form:
```tsx
const [email, setEmail] = useState("");
const [password, setPassword] = useState("");
const [showPassword, setShowPassword] = useState(false);
const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);
const [submitting, setSubmitting] = useState(false);

if (status === "loading") return <View style={...}><ActivityIndicator color={colors.primary} /></View>;
if (status === "authenticated") return <Redirect href="/" />;

async function handleSubmit() {
  setError(null);
  if (!email.trim() || !password) { setError("Renseignez votre email et votre mot de passe."); return; }
  setSubmitting(true);
  try { await signIn(email, password); router.replace("/"); }
  catch (err) { setError(err instanceof ApiError ? err.message : "Connexion impossible."); }
  finally { setSubmitting(false); }
}
```
Note: after signIn, status becomes authenticated, so the component re-renders and `<Redirect>` triggers; `router.replace` may be redundant. Keep one. Use `router.replace("/")` only, but status change triggers redirect. Both okay. Could omit router. But after signIn resolves, state updated, redirect happens. Keep `router.replace("/")` for clarity; no harm.

TextInput `autoCapitalize="none"`, `keyboardType="email-address"`, `autoComplete="email"`, `textContentType="emailAddress"`, `returnKeyType="next"`, password `secureTextEntry={!showPassword}`.

